From 496d4864b8c9ca54f340d0e80c62c2f81c68f29d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Oreo.Yang" <2167young@163.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:09:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] validation FEATURE incremental validation driven by an edit
 diff

Validating a whole module after every edit is quadratic in the size of the
datastore, which dominates the cost of provisioning thousands of instances.

Classify every when/must/leafref/unique constraint of a module by how far its
dependencies reach (local, list-scope, bounded, unbounded) and cache the result
per context. Given a diff that describes every change made since the data were
last valid, lyd_validate_module_incr() then revalidates only the subtrees the
diff can have invalidated. Anything the classifier cannot reduce to a finite
set of paths - schema mounts included - falls back to full validation, so the
verdict is always identical to validating the whole module.

lyd_validate_incr_stats() reports the call and fallback counters, per context
or for the whole process, since a context does not survive a schema change.
